# Production build config (used by `npm run build`, i.e. Vite "production" mode).
#
# Same value as dev: the UI always calls /api on its own origin. In dev, Vite's
# server.proxy forwards it (vite.config.ts); in production, the Cloudflare Pages
# Function in functions/api/ forwards it. Either way the browser only ever talks
# to the origin it was served from, so no CORS and no backend URL in the bundle.
#
# The real backend URL is the API_ORIGIN secret on the Cloudflare Pages project:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put API_ORIGIN --project-name=<your-project>
#
# To point a build straight at a backend instead (bypassing the proxy), set
# VITE_API_BASE_URL to an absolute URL — but note it is then baked into the JS
# bundle and public to anyone loading the site.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
